#!/usr/bin/env python3
#
# cachy-auto-update-tray: the icon in the system tray
#
# Started by the desktop's autostart in every graphical session, as the user.
# It shows whether updates are waiting, and a click installs them: it asks
# systemd to start cachy-auto-update-now.service, and that run brings its own
# progress bar. The menu can also show the log in a terminal, look for updates
# again, or open the settings.
#
# It talks to the tray directly over D-Bus: StatusNotifierItem for the icon,
# com.canonical.dbusmenu for its menu. That needs only the GLib bindings the
# progress bar uses anyway, not a whole widget toolkit.
#
# Copyright (C) 2026 Felitendo
# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later

